# swiss-mc — optional live-odds provider keys (DX-05)
#
# The app runs RATING-ONLY without any of these — the first sim needs NO API key and shows a
# `live odds off (no ODDSPAPI_KEY) — using manual ratings` banner (fail-soft, never crashes).
# These keys are Phase-5 / v1+ enhancements that back-solve per-team ratings from market odds.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values you have. `.env` is gitignored — NEVER
# commit real keys. Leave any provider blank to keep it off.

# OddsPapi (Pinnacle-backed esports odds) — the primary provider.
ODDSPAPI_KEY=

# The Odds API (soccer_fifa_world_cup: Pinnacle + Betfair 1X2) — the World Cup sharp reference
# used to calibrate the goals model. Get a key at the-odds-api.com. Read only in scripts/ via
# load_dotenv(); NEVER commit the real key (.env is gitignored). Prefer setting it as an
# environment variable / secret in the cloud environment settings over pasting it into chat.
THE_ODDS_API_KEY=

# Polymarket (prediction-market odds) — optional.
POLYMARKET_API_KEY=

# Kalshi (regulated event contracts).
#
# READING markets (current betting options for the EV monitor) is KEYLESS — no key needed; the
# monitor fetches public market data with no credentials. The API key is only required to (a) read
# your real account BALANCE so Kelly stakes size against your true bankroll
# (`scripts.ev_report --use-balance`), and (b) sign reads. Order placement is NOT implemented
# (read-only monitor; execution gated behind [Q-LEGAL]).
#
# Kalshi's current auth is RSA request-signing and needs BOTH halves:
#   1. the API Key ID (a UUID — the public half). The repo also accepts the literal var name
#      `Kalshi` (what the owner set in the cloud env). Prefer the explicit name below.
#   2. the RSA PRIVATE KEY (PEM) that signs requests — set it INLINE or via a file PATH.
# NEVER commit the private key (.env is gitignored). Prefer cloud-env secrets over pasting keys.
#
# NETWORK: live reads need `api.elections.kalshi.com` on the environment's egress allowlist.
KALSHI_API_KEY_ID=
# Inline PEM (literal \n between lines is accepted), OR point KALSHI_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH at a file:
KALSHI_PRIVATE_KEY=
KALSHI_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=
# Optional, only if the PEM is passphrase-encrypted (Kalshi-issued keys usually are not):
KALSHI_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD=

# Legacy slot kept for back-compat (the back-solved CS2 ratings path); the WC monitor uses the
# RSA pair above.
KALSHI_API_KEY=

# PandaScore (live FINISHED-series results) — optional FALLBACK A for the live-results seam (RES-01).
# The bo3.gg primary results source is KEYLESS, so the first run (and the recorded-fixture tests)
# need NO key. Leave blank to skip the PandaScore fallback — scripts/fetch_results.py degrades to
# bo3.gg-only, never crashes. NEVER commit a real key (.env is gitignored).
PANDASCORE_KEY=
